hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2867","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adiyy and Muhammad ibn Ja'far and 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid, from 'Awf ibn Abi Jamīlah, from Ziyād ibn Ḥaṣīn, who narrated to us Abū al-'Āliyah, who said:\n\nIbn 'Abbās (RA) told me that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said on the morning of the Day of 'Aqabah:\n\nIbn Abi 'Adiyy mentioned in his narration, and likewise 'Awf said:\n\n\Bring me some pebbles","\"" which are the pebbles used for throwing (ramy). When they were placed in his hand"," he (ﷺ) said:\n\n\""With such as these"," with such as these. Beware of going to extremes in religion"," for those who came before you were destroyed only by going to extremes in religion.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"2868","###\n Bundar narrated to us another time with the same wording, except that he said: \Ziyad bin Husain narrated to me.\"" And [also] Bundar narrated to us: Yahya bin Sa'id narrated to us"," Auf narrated to us"," Ziyad bin Husain narrated to me"," Abu al-'Aliyah said: Ibn 'Abbas (RA) said to me. Auf said: \""I do not know whether it was Al-Fadl or 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas (RA) who said"""
